UID:5e5de8962468bfd2@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260914T011642Z
SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T205000
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 7:30 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 7:15 PM.\nOn stage: 8:10 PM–8:50 PM.\nACT II
  Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — p
 roduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dan
 cers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Ti
 me.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgi
 ving and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are ca
 lled unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedu
 le\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mas
 ter: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-
 N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Flowers ***\nFlower
 s — Costume (you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Pink Bloomers\; Shoe
 s: Pink Pointe Shoes w/ ribbons & elastics (clean\, quiet\, unpancacked)
  *Dancers of Color may wear flesh-tone Pointe Shoes\; Makeup: Full Stage
  Makeup\; Hair: French Twist\; Accessories (BA provides): Headpiece\nFul
 l Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Apply foundation and powder match
 ing skintone\n• Light skin tone eye shadow over entire eye\n• Dark b
 rown eye shadow over crease\n• Medium brown eye shadow blended over br
 own\n• Black fake eyelashes (note: apply mascara to own lashes before 
 application of fake lashes)\n• Apply eyeliner after lashes dry\n• Bl
 ush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look wash
 ed out in the stage lights)\n• Brown or tan on contour cheekbones\, ha
 irline\n• Use a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n•
  Red or Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights a
 nd flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costum
 e pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\
 n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at t
 he point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n• Never throw costu
 mes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic stra
 ps\n• Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n• Do not a
 ttempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n
 • Never apply stage make-up while in costume and shall take great care
  to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n• Ref
 rain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n• Neve
 r wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n• Do not handle or con
 sume food or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n
 • Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from th
 e theater\n• Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs
  following their use\n• Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n
 • Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe
  policies\n• Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything
  that may damage or stain costumes.
